//! Stable shell execution policy delivered with the tool, across roles and models.

pub(super) const DESCRIPTION: &str = "Run a POSIX shell command. Start defaults to sandbox_access=isolated. Execution environment: isolated uses the configured filesystem sandbox, private HOME, filtered environment variables, and isolated networking. network allows host networking for this command while keeping the same filesystem mounts, private HOME, and filtered environment; it does not restore host configuration, credentials, agent sockets, or environment variables. unsandboxed removes filesystem/network isolation and inherits the evorch process environment (which may differ from a login terminal), with explicit tool environment overrides. Select the narrowest mode that supplies the resources the command actually needs: network for connectivity alone, unsandboxed when host files, configuration, credentials, sockets, or environment are needed. You may request the appropriate mode directly when that need is already known. Both network and unsandboxed require a nonempty justification and review before execution; review may be automatic or require a user response, or escalation may be disabled. A request is not an approval. Failure diagnosis: an error describes this command in its selected execution environment, not the whole host. Distinguish connectivity, filesystem access, HOME/configuration, environment, authentication, and command failures. Before declaring a resource missing or asking the user to install, log in, supply secrets, or run the command manually, check whether isolation hides it and use the reviewed access path when justified by the user's task. Do not repeat a deterministic failure under unchanged conditions or reset unrelated configuration. If review denies the request, use the exact returned reason; do not assume a GUI prompt, user refusal, timeout, or missing capability, and do not bypass the denial. Without yield_ms, wait for completion. Start with yield_ms (0..60000) to return a run-owned job ID and cursor; use action poll/stdin/stop to continue it. Poll accepts yield_ms up to 1800000 (30 minutes) and returns early on new output or completion; stdin/stop accept up to 60000. Jobs retain their sandbox/cwd/environment, stop when the run ends, and cannot resume after restart. Live output contains complete lines; long output has a bounded temporary artifact on completion. Control actions retain the job's original access and cannot set sandbox_access; stdin for a reviewed job requires a fresh review.";

pub(super) const ACCESS_DESCRIPTION: &str = "Start only. isolated: configured filesystem/network isolation, private HOME, filtered environment. network: reviewed host networking only; filesystem mounts, private HOME, and filtered environment stay isolated, so host configuration/credentials/sockets are not restored. unsandboxed: reviewed host filesystem/network access and inherited evorch process environment. Choose by required resources, not just the command's name. network and unsandboxed require a nonempty justification; denial is returned with its reason.";
